# Experiments T/L (2026-10-08): EKF3 fuses AprilTag fixes as ExternalNav (tag_bridge.py, ODOMETRY on SERIAL1), with
# optical flow (VELXY 5) and rangefinder height (POSZ 2) in the SAME source set (verified in source: AID_ABSOLUTE once a
# tag arrives; flow keeps fusing; METHODOLOGY "T design"). Loaded AFTER gnss_denied_nomag.parm.
VISO_TYPE 1             # MAVLink visual odometry (AP_VisualOdom_MAV)
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 6        # ExternalNav (the tag fixes)
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6          # ExternalNav yaw (tag yaw). YAW 0 would leave yaw never aligned (filter unhealthy in AID_ABSOLUTE)
VISO_YAW_M_NSE 0.05     # rad; with EKF3's 5 deg floor the effective yaw sigma is 5 deg (the heading-path setting)
VISO_POS_M_NSE 0.05     # m; = sent sigma_pos (tag characterisation: central-third fixes p95 40 mm at 2.26 m), so effective = 0.05
VISO_QUAL_MIN 0
VISO_DELAY_MS 15        # = round(min VISP receipt - capture): 15.6 ms (tag_check1c), 15.0 ms (tag_check2); D20 rule (receipt measure). The node measure (a) is 4 ms: (a)/(b) disagree by 11 ms, reported
ARMING_SKIPCHK 262144   # skip ONLY check bit 18 (VisualOdometry): the downward camera cannot see a tag on the ground (it is
                        # below the floor plane at rest); simulator truth flies these trials. (This build renamed ARMING_CHECK
                        # to ARMING_SKIPCHK, a skip-bitmask: AP_Arming.cpp:195-201; found when ARMING_CHECK did not read back.)
